// `mod.NAME` reaches functions only, so a module-level `pub val` used to be reported as "module
// 'number' has no function 'float_min_positive'" -- which sends the reader looking for a function
// that was never the point. The name is right; the form is wrong, and `use number.float_min_positive`
// followed by the bare name is what works. Two reviews asked for this separately (C20).
use number

fn main() {
    print(format("{}", number.float_min_positive))
}
